WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.112
The applied project combines several concepts.

00:00:03.112 --> 00:00:05.907
We sequence admissions for each patient.

00:00:05.907 --> 00:00:08.732
LAG retrieves the previous discharge.

00:00:08.732 --> 00:00:11.722
A second CTE calculates the gap.

00:00:11.722 --> 00:00:18.537
The final query joins patient names and classifies whether the new admission occurred within thirty days.

00:00:18.537 --> 00:00:22.097
This is a practical sequence-analysis pipeline.

00:00:22.097 --> 00:00:28.287
Connect this idea to a sales team calculating running revenue and top products by region.

00:00:28.287 --> 00:00:34.177
Ask what could go wrong if the concept were misunderstood: could rows be duplicated,

00:00:34.177 --> 00:00:41.777
important records disappear, categories be interpreted incorrectly, or a report become difficult to reproduce?

00:00:41.777 --> 00:00:47.697
A strong analyst can explain both the SQL operation and the assumption behind it.

00:00:47.697 --> 00:00:53.637
After the example, summarize the idea in one plain-language sentence before moving on.
